    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "fc54635f1b7104778d00ff91470ce26b670243f2232c9954509be80bedba486e",
      "text": "Pasochoa is an extinct volcano with very fertile lands enriched by prehistoric eruptions that released minerals and ash, now serving as excellent natural fertilizer. In the Andean forests and wetlands here, one can find a great diversity of plants, trees, animals, and insects.\n\nOur trek will take around 6–7 hours. After reaching the summit of Pasochoa (4200 m), we’ll head to our lodge for some rest.\n\nFree time and overnight stay.\n\nAccommodation: Hacienda Los Mortiños www.losmortinos.com \t\n\nMeals: Box lunch, dinner",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1aMNBOgd-6s71uwS-aEM_gfDEmhLQHHzx",
        "documentSha256": "7c5d98482c31f50b5ee1a0833d504bfd399821348a9b7fe122728d6546d59b4d",
